From 57d040a4c99e61a81fda0131dbb341f8156ffe7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:27:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: say why the firmware could not be loaded

The most common reason for the VPU not coming up on a board with a
non-default firmware is a mismatch between the image and the reserved
memory region the device tree gives it: a Gen2 image needs 0x700000
bytes of memory, a Gen1 image 0x500000. iris_load_fw_to_memory() failed
that check with a bare -EINVAL and no message, so the only trace was
the generic "firmware download failed -22".

Print the image name, its size in memory and the size of the region when
it does not fit, and print which HFI generation was detected and how
much of the region is used when it does, so a wrong or mis-sized
firmware is recognisable from the log without a debugger.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XHbRyvZ53xawh6pBdmacMe
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_firmware.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_firmware.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_firmware.c
index af178a438..f4ba2d188 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_firmware.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_firmware.c
@@ -163,10 +163,16 @@ static int iris_load_fw_to_memory(struct iris_core *core)
 
 	fw_size = qcom_mdt_get_size(firmware);
 	if (fw_size < 0 || res_size < (size_t)fw_size) {
+		dev_err(dev, "firmware %s needs %zd bytes but the reserved memory region has %zu\n",
+			fw_name, fw_size, res_size);
 		ret = -EINVAL;
 		goto err_release_fw;
 	}
 
+	dev_info(dev, "firmware %s: %s HFI, %zd of %zu bytes of reserved memory\n", fw_name,
+		 core->iris_firmware_data == &iris_hfi_gen2_data ? "Gen2" : "Gen1",
+		 fw_size, res_size);
+
 	mem_virt = memremap(mem_phys, res_size, MEMREMAP_WC);
 	if (!mem_virt) {
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
-- 
